.TH GIT-PERMS 1 "2026-06-02" "git-perms 0.0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-perms \- store and restore Unix file permissions across git operations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git perms
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.br
.B git-perms
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-perms
records full Unix file modes for git-tracked files in a committed
.I .gitperms
file.
It restores those modes after operations that otherwise preserve only git's
executable bit, such as clone, checkout, merge, or rebase.
.PP
The binary is normally invoked as the
.B git perms
subcommand.
The standalone
.B git-perms
name is also available.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B save
Scan git-tracked files and write their permissions to
.IR .gitperms .
Existing entries for files no longer tracked are removed.
.TP
.B restore
Read
.I .gitperms
and apply the stored modes to files in the working tree.
Missing files are skipped with a warning.
.TP
.B diff
Show permission differences between
.I .gitperms
and the filesystem.
Exits with status 1 when differences exist.
.TP
.BI "diff --quiet"
Check for permission differences without printing them.
Exits with status 1 when differences exist.
.TP
.B hook install
Install hooks that automatically save and restore permissions:
.BR pre\-commit ,
.BR post\-checkout ,
.BR post\-merge ,
and
.BR post\-rewrite .